  "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B006",
        "laureates": [
          "Hidetoshi Katori",
          "Jun Ye"
        ],
        "citation": "for the invention and development of optical lattice clocks"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B019",
    "B005"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B006 remains the strongest final configuration because it identifies a discrete instrument principle whose experimental consequences are exceptionally mature: magic-wavelength confinement made it possible to interrogate many atoms while controlling the dominant trapping shift. The resulting clocks have been independently reproduced and have opened quantitatively new capabilities in time-frequency metrology, geodesy, and tests of fundamental physics. The proposed attribution remains unusually coherent: Katori supplied the foundational lattice-clock concept, and Ye made decisive contributions to its experimental development into a stringent precision platform.",
    "case_against": "The citation must remain restricted to optical lattice clocks and must not absorb the broader history of optical-frequency metrology, single-ion clocks, or later performance refinements by many groups. A final historical review is still needed to test whether Katori and Ye fully represent the indispensable conceptual and experimental contributions.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "olsson-eva",
        "point": "Olsson argues that B019 is a discrete, experimentally verified instrumental invention, while maintaining that Rose, Urban, and Haider may form the necessary chain from electron-optical concepts to reliable realization.",
        "response": "I agree that B019 is a serious and mature alternative whose transformation of what can be measured is unmistakable. However, the unresolved distinction among correction theory, robust realization, dissemination, and later instrument development is central to exact credit. Until the documentary record establishes that all three proposed names made original prize-defining contributions, B006 has the firmer attribution and more sharply bounded physical principle."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson favors B005 because Cirac and Zoller have clean two-person credit for foundational proposals realized across controllable atomic platforms.",
        "response": "The attribution for B005 is indeed unusually attractive, and the proposals had profound generative influence. I remain persuaded, however, that its trapped-ion computing and optical-lattice simulation components require a more difficult demonstration of unity as one delimited achievement. B006 is a completed and independently reproducible measurement invention, with a direct causal path from its central idea to an established capability."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "eriksson-olle",
        "point": "Eriksson regards B017 as a decades-tested transformation of first-principles materials prediction, but recognizes questions about combining distinct methods and assigning implementation credit.",
        "response": "I accept the exceptional practical reach of B017. The acknowledged difficulty of treating ultrasoft pseudopotentials, PAW, and practical implementation as one indivisible achievement, however, reinforces the value of B006's narrower conceptual and experimental boundary. Its performance can be directly benchmarked across laboratories without making a broad computational ecosystem the object of the prize."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether historical evidence supports attributing the decisive invention and development of optical lattice clocks solely to Katori and Ye.",
      "How best to define the citation so it excludes single-ion clocks, wider optical-frequency metrology, and later performance refinements while retaining the full significance of the lattice-clock principle."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "I have institutional connections through Swedish quantum-technology networks, including WACQT's Chalmers-led environment, but no candidate-specific collaboration, financial interest, or other conflict requiring recusal is apparent from the supplied evidence."
  }
}
